WEBVTT

00:00:00.341 --> 00:00:02.044
Last video ended with a question:

00:00:02.685 --> 00:00:05.451
where is a derivative positive, and where is

00:00:05.511 --> 00:00:06.092
it negative?

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:07.512
We'll come back to that.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.631
First, picture a hike.

00:00:10.216 --> 00:00:12.342
This curve is the trail's height as you

00:00:12.384 --> 00:00:12.904
walk along it.

00:00:13.528 --> 00:00:16.097
Its tangent is flat in two places, at

00:00:16.279 --> 00:00:18.426
x equals zero and at x equals three.

00:00:19.272 --> 00:00:22.060
At three, the curve turns, from falling to

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:22.502
rising.

00:00:22.944 --> 00:00:24.175
That's the creek at the bottom of the

00:00:24.197 --> 00:00:24.438
valley.

00:00:25.166 --> 00:00:26.793
But at zero it doesn't turn.

00:00:27.276 --> 00:00:28.903
It levels off for an instant, like a

00:00:28.984 --> 00:00:31.254
flat ledge on the way down, then keeps

00:00:31.315 --> 00:00:31.676
falling.

00:00:32.462 --> 00:00:34.757
So what decides whether the curve turns?

00:00:35.437 --> 00:00:37.050
Start with what you know from Year 11.

00:00:38.056 --> 00:00:40.820
Where the derivative is positive, the tangent slopes

00:00:41.001 --> 00:00:42.904
up, and the curve is increasing:

00:00:43.466 --> 00:00:45.849
its height goes up as x increases.

00:00:46.611 --> 00:00:48.618
Where the derivative is negative, the curve is

00:00:48.679 --> 00:00:49.220
decreasing.

00:00:50.046 --> 00:00:52.160
Watch the tangent move along this curve.

00:00:52.705 --> 00:00:55.009
Its gradient is negative all the way to

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:58.054
x equals three, except for one instant at

00:00:58.116 --> 00:01:00.078
zero, where it's exactly zero.

00:01:00.926 --> 00:01:02.158
After three it's positive.

00:01:02.943 --> 00:01:05.230
Let's record just the sign, in a strip

00:01:05.371 --> 00:01:05.752
underneath.

00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:07.710
Two words to keep apart.

00:01:08.417 --> 00:01:10.645
A stationary point is any point where the

00:01:10.666 --> 00:01:13.657
derivative is zero, so the tangent is horizontal.

00:01:14.161 --> 00:01:14.986
That's all it says.

00:01:15.911 --> 00:01:17.978
A turning point is where the curve changes

00:01:18.039 --> 00:01:18.519
direction.

00:01:19.121 --> 00:01:21.862
It's either a local maximum, higher than every

00:01:21.943 --> 00:01:23.143
nearby point on the curve,

00:01:23.844 --> 00:01:26.485
or a local minimum, lower than every nearby

00:01:26.546 --> 00:01:26.745
point.

00:01:27.529 --> 00:01:30.025
Local means compared only with points close by.

00:01:30.871 --> 00:01:32.920
So the point at three is stationary,

00:01:33.423 --> 00:01:34.528
and it's a turning point.

00:01:35.152 --> 00:01:37.725
The point at zero is stationary, but it's

00:01:37.866 --> 00:01:38.810
not a turning point.

00:01:39.502 --> 00:01:40.495
So what decides it?

00:01:41.041 --> 00:01:43.439
The sign of the derivative on each side.

00:01:44.163 --> 00:01:46.206
If the curve rises into the point and

00:01:46.388 --> 00:01:48.813
falls after it, the sign goes from plus

00:01:48.894 --> 00:01:49.414
to minus.

00:01:50.077 --> 00:01:52.545
Nothing nearby is higher, so it's a local

00:01:52.606 --> 00:01:53.006
maximum.

00:01:53.971 --> 00:01:56.238
If it falls in and rises out, that's

00:01:56.358 --> 00:01:57.261
minus to plus,

00:01:57.763 --> 00:02:00.391
and nothing nearby is lower: a local minimum.

00:02:00.993 --> 00:02:02.253
And if the sign is the same on

00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:04.915
both sides, plus and plus, or minus and

00:02:04.936 --> 00:02:07.377
minus, the curve keeps going the same way.

00:02:07.981 --> 00:02:10.196
That's called a horizontal point of inflection.

00:02:10.741 --> 00:02:13.038
It's stationary, but it isn't a turning point.

00:02:13.688 --> 00:02:15.914
Why does our curve turn at three but

00:02:15.975 --> 00:02:16.656
not at zero?

00:02:17.339 --> 00:02:20.285
Its derivative is four x squared, times x

00:02:20.346 --> 00:02:22.089
minus three, graphed underneath.

00:02:22.772 --> 00:02:24.500
The sign of f prime is whether this

00:02:24.521 --> 00:02:26.550
graph is above or below the axis.

00:02:27.315 --> 00:02:29.404
At three, it crosses the axis, so the

00:02:29.445 --> 00:02:31.313
sign changes from minus to plus.

00:02:32.077 --> 00:02:33.965
At zero, it only touches the axis.

00:02:34.468 --> 00:02:36.754
The factor x squared is never negative, so

00:02:36.775 --> 00:02:38.038
it doesn't change the sign there,

00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:40.826
and x minus three is negative on both

00:02:40.888 --> 00:02:41.609
sides of zero.

00:02:42.412 --> 00:02:44.721
And because this derivative graph is unbroken, its

00:02:44.762 --> 00:02:47.051
sign can only change where it equals zero.

00:02:47.755 --> 00:02:50.023
So one test value in each interval is

00:02:50.084 --> 00:02:50.284
enough.

00:02:51.176 --> 00:02:52.462
Let's turn that into a method.

00:02:53.146 --> 00:02:55.849
Find and classify the stationary points of f

00:02:56.191 --> 00:02:59.095
of x equals two x cubed, minus nine

00:02:59.196 --> 00:03:01.519
x squared, plus twelve x, minus three.

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:05.189
First differentiate, and factorise as far as you

00:03:05.231 --> 00:03:05.390
can.

00:03:06.153 --> 00:03:08.236
f prime of x is six x squared,

00:03:08.397 --> 00:03:11.301
minus eighteen x, plus twelve, which is six,

00:03:11.583 --> 00:03:14.207
times x minus one, times x minus two.

00:03:14.909 --> 00:03:17.334
So f prime is zero at x equals

00:03:17.476 --> 00:03:19.099
one and x equals two.

00:03:19.802 --> 00:03:22.028
Those two values split the number line into

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:22.851
three intervals.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:26.773
Now test one easy value inside each interval.

00:03:27.541 --> 00:03:28.529
Only the sign matters.

00:03:29.398 --> 00:03:29.941
At zero,

00:03:30.445 --> 00:03:32.197
f prime is twelve, positive.

00:03:32.962 --> 00:03:35.152
At one point five, it's minus one point

00:03:35.193 --> 00:03:36.197
five, negative.

00:03:36.962 --> 00:03:39.190
At three, it's twelve, positive.

00:03:39.893 --> 00:03:42.582
So f increases for x less than one

00:03:43.025 --> 00:03:44.349
and for x greater than two,

00:03:44.932 --> 00:03:46.236
and decreases in between.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.166
Plus to minus at one gives a local

00:03:49.247 --> 00:03:49.687
maximum,

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:52.096
and minus to plus at two gives a

00:03:52.157 --> 00:03:52.798
local minimum.

00:03:53.564 --> 00:03:55.860
For the heights, use f, not f prime.

00:03:56.684 --> 00:03:57.667
f of one is two,

00:03:58.169 --> 00:03:59.332
and f of two is one.

00:03:59.988 --> 00:04:01.112
Back to our first curve,

00:04:01.675 --> 00:04:03.521
f of x equals x to the fourth,

00:04:03.642 --> 00:04:04.906
minus four x cubed.

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:08.595
Its derivative, four x squared times x minus

00:04:08.676 --> 00:04:08.995
three,

00:04:09.577 --> 00:04:12.582
is zero at x equals zero and three.

00:04:13.305 --> 00:04:14.228
Test minus one:

00:04:14.871 --> 00:04:15.573
minus sixteen.

00:04:16.177 --> 00:04:16.719
Test one:

00:04:17.344 --> 00:04:17.805
minus eight.

00:04:18.492 --> 00:04:19.157
Test four:

00:04:19.743 --> 00:04:20.246
sixty-four.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.076
Minus, then minus, around zero.

00:04:23.699 --> 00:04:25.803
The sign doesn't change, so the point zero,

00:04:25.885 --> 00:04:28.230
zero is a horizontal point of inflection.

00:04:29.233 --> 00:04:31.896
Minus to plus at three gives a local

00:04:31.957 --> 00:04:32.277
minimum,

00:04:32.799 --> 00:04:35.262
and f of three is eighty-one minus one

00:04:35.323 --> 00:04:37.405
hundred and eight, which is minus twenty-seven.

00:04:37.907 --> 00:04:39.612
Now last video's quotient,

00:04:40.135 --> 00:04:42.000
y equals e to the x, over x

00:04:42.041 --> 00:04:44.166
plus one, with x not equal to minus

00:04:44.228 --> 00:04:44.327
one.

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:47.222
Its derivative is x e to the x,

00:04:47.424 --> 00:04:49.092
over x plus one, all squared.

00:04:49.775 --> 00:04:51.218
e to the x and the squared bracket

00:04:51.259 --> 00:04:53.545
are both positive, so the derivative has the

00:04:53.586 --> 00:04:54.127
sign of x:

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:56.334
negative, negative, then positive.

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:58.966
So there's a local minimum at zero, one.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:02.242
But minus one isn't in the domain, so

00:05:02.284 --> 00:05:03.328
it's not a stationary point.

00:05:04.013 --> 00:05:06.124
It still splits the chart, because the curve

00:05:06.165 --> 00:05:06.667
breaks there.

00:05:07.251 --> 00:05:09.376
The function decreases on each side of minus

00:05:09.518 --> 00:05:10.860
one, but not across it.

00:05:11.584 --> 00:05:12.285
At minus two, y

00:05:12.788 --> 00:05:15.337
is about minus point one four, and at

00:05:15.378 --> 00:05:17.424
minus a half, it's about one point two

00:05:17.546 --> 00:05:17.645
one.

00:05:18.259 --> 00:05:19.150
Here's a way to picture it.

00:05:19.576 --> 00:05:21.882
Turn the signs into arrows, and the arrows

00:05:22.124 --> 00:05:22.885
sketch the shape.

00:05:23.468 --> 00:05:25.876
Plus is an arrow up, minus is an

00:05:25.957 --> 00:05:26.478
arrow down.

00:05:27.222 --> 00:05:28.830
Up then down draws a peak.

00:05:29.314 --> 00:05:31.101
Down then up draws a valley.

00:05:31.705 --> 00:05:33.670
Two arrows the same way draw a step,

00:05:33.992 --> 00:05:35.616
the horizontal point of inflection.

00:05:36.239 --> 00:05:39.370
Just never join arrows across an excluded value.

00:05:39.633 --> 00:05:40.747
There, you lift your pen.

00:05:43.526 --> 00:05:43.913
Your turn.

00:05:44.441 --> 00:05:46.845
For f of x equals x cubed, minus

00:05:46.925 --> 00:05:49.829
three x, find where f is increasing and

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:50.871
where it's decreasing.

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:53.791
Then find and classify its stationary points.

00:05:54.415 --> 00:05:55.236
Pause here to answer.

00:06:07.988 --> 00:06:10.511
f prime of x is three, times x

00:06:10.573 --> 00:06:12.756
minus one, times x plus one,

00:06:13.338 --> 00:06:15.621
so it's zero at minus one and one.

00:06:16.324 --> 00:06:19.571
Testing minus two, zero and two gives plus,

00:06:19.773 --> 00:06:20.514
minus, plus.

00:06:21.136 --> 00:06:23.781
So f increases for x less than minus

00:06:23.882 --> 00:06:26.767
one or greater than one, and decreases in

00:06:26.808 --> 00:06:27.188
between.

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:30.435
There's a local maximum at minus one, two,

00:06:30.877 --> 00:06:33.102
and a local minimum at one, minus two.

00:06:33.786 --> 00:06:34.597
The heights come from f.

00:06:35.468 --> 00:06:37.523
Using f prime gives zero every time.

00:06:39.192 --> 00:06:39.598
Last one.

00:06:40.268 --> 00:06:42.934
A function has derivative f prime of x

00:06:43.216 --> 00:06:46.463
equals x, times the bracket x minus two,

00:06:46.625 --> 00:06:47.065
squared.

00:06:47.827 --> 00:06:50.149
Find the x values of its stationary points,

00:06:50.551 --> 00:06:53.313
and classify each one, using the sign of

00:06:53.554 --> 00:06:53.973
f prime.

00:06:54.798 --> 00:06:55.683
Pause here to answer.

00:07:06.416 --> 00:07:08.606
f prime is zero at x equals zero

00:07:08.748 --> 00:07:09.692
and x equals two.

00:07:10.478 --> 00:07:11.302
Test minus one:

00:07:11.927 --> 00:07:13.234
minus nine, negative.

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:16.430
Tests at one and three are both positive.

00:07:17.014 --> 00:07:19.430
So at zero it's minus to plus, a

00:07:19.471 --> 00:07:20.054
local minimum.

00:07:20.778 --> 00:07:22.664
At two it's plus on both sides.

00:07:23.227 --> 00:07:25.436
The squared bracket doesn't change the sign, so

00:07:25.517 --> 00:07:27.505
that's a horizontal point of inflection, not a

00:07:27.546 --> 00:07:28.067
turning point.

00:07:28.752 --> 00:07:30.585
Don't assume a minimum has to be followed

00:07:30.626 --> 00:07:31.190
by a maximum.

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:35.003
So the sign of the derivative on each

00:07:35.083 --> 00:07:37.746
side tells you whether a stationary point turns.

00:07:38.592 --> 00:07:39.964
Next, a bigger question.

00:07:40.668 --> 00:07:43.211
Here's attempt one's curve again, with its local

00:07:43.271 --> 00:07:44.172
maximum of two.

00:07:44.873 --> 00:07:47.036
But on the interval from minus two to

00:07:47.096 --> 00:07:47.456
three,

00:07:48.057 --> 00:07:50.300
is two the largest value the function reaches?

00:07:52.928 --> 00:07:53.791
Here are the key notes.

00:07:54.194 --> 00:07:55.741
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:55.783 --> 00:07:56.244
to copy them.
